--- log ---
2026-05-01T10:00Z claude created — supersedes 0141 per design discussion

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0141 proposed grouping cloud+local providers under one logical model entry.
This ticket adopts the cleaner decision from design discussion: keep one entry per
*deployed instance* (a specific router+endpoint combination), and align the schema
with the OpenAI / liteLLM field conventions.

The key field clarifications:
- `name` → renamed `Name`: instance identifier used in experiments register and
  `experiments.toml` sweep references (e.g. `"qwen3.5:35b"`, `"qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b"`).
- NEW `display_name`: human-readable label used in figures and paper tables
  (e.g. `"Qwen 3.5 35B (local)"` → `"Qwen 3.5 35B"`). No router provenance in
  display name; that belongs in figure captions.
- NEW `base_url`: API endpoint string, replacing the `router` enum. Makes every
  instance directly callable via the OpenAI SDK / liteLLM with zero adapter code.
  Examples: `"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"` (OpenRouter),
  `"http://localhost:11434/v1"` (Ollama).
- `router_model` → renamed `model_id`: the OpenAI-format model string passed to
  the API. Already present; rename makes the liteLLM semantics explicit.

Retiring the `router` enum removes the last place that requires provider-specific
dispatch logic in the runner.

Relation to 0141: Close 0141 as `won't do` after this ticket ships.

## Proposed schema (one entry, post-migration)

```yaml
- name: "qwen3.5:35b"              # instance key — used in experiments.toml
  display_name: "Qwen 3.5 35B"     # label for figures and tables
  base_url: "http://localhost:11434/v1"
  model_id: "qwen3.5:35b"          # OpenAI-format model string
  provider: Alibaba
  country: CN
  architecture: moe
  context_window: 131072
  price_per_mtok_in: 0.0
  price_per_mtok_out: 0.0
  size_class: medium
  license: open-apache
```

Cloud example:
```yaml
- name: "qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b"
  display_name: "Qwen 3.5 35B"
  base_url: "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
  model_id: "qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b"
  provider: Alibaba
  country: CN
  architecture: moe
  context_window: 262144
  price_per_mtok_in: 0.16
  price_per_mtok_out: 1.3
  params: "35B MoE (3B active)"
  size_class: medium
  license: open-apache
  web_search: true
```

## Actions

1. Update `models.yaml`:
   - Rename `id` → `name`, `name` → `display_name` throughout.
   - Add `base_url` to every entry (OpenRouter URL or `http://localhost:11434/v1`).
   - Rename `router_model` → `model_id`.
   - Remove `router` field from every entry.
   - Keep all other fields (provider, country, architecture, etc.) unchanged.
   - Update the header comment (entry count, date).

2. Update the loader/parser (`experiments/` code that reads `models.yaml`):
   - Accept new field names; reject unknown top-level keys (strict mode).
   - Build `ModelInstance` dataclass with `name`, `display_name`, `base_url`,
     `model_id`, and remaining metadata fields.
   - Use `base_url` + `model_id` to construct the OpenAI client call; no more
     `router` dispatch branch.

3. Update `experiments.toml` sweep entries: replace any remaining uses of
   old field names in sweep references.

4. Update all downstream code that reads `model.name` or `model.id` to use
   `model.name` (instance key) vs `model.display_name` (figures).
   Specifically: figure-generation scripts must use `display_name`.

5. Update tests in `experiments/tests/` to reflect new schema.

6. Close ticket 0141 as `won't do` with cross-reference to this ticket.

## Test

- `pytest experiments/tests/test_registry.py` — all entries parse; ModelInstance
  fields populated; no `router` field present; `base_url` non-empty on all entries.
- Dry-run sweep: runner constructs API calls using `base_url` + `model_id`; no
  router-dispatch code path exercised.
- Figure script smoke test: labels use `display_name` not `name`.

## Exit criteria

- `models.yaml` uses `name`, `display_name`, `base_url`, `model_id` throughout.
- Runner has zero `router`-dispatch branches.
- All figures use `display_name` for axis/legend labels.
- Tests green; ticket 0141 closed.
